--- PRC-27, 28: symbolic link ---
a text called scratch is "{'the workspace'}/procpayload1".
open a file for writing called 'scratch scribe' at scratch.
Write "payload" to 'scratch scribe'.
Close 'scratch scribe'.
a text called 'scratch link path' is "{'the workspace'}/proclink1".
Create symbolic link from "procpayload1" to 'scratch link path'.
If 'scratch link path' is not available then, Print "ASSERT PRC-27: expected available got missing", Exit 95. Print "resolves".
a text called 'scratch dangling path' is "{'the workspace'}/procdangling1".
Create symbolic link from "procmissing1" to 'scratch dangling path'.
If 'scratch dangling path' is available then, Print "ASSERT PRC-27: expected missing got available", Exit 95. Print "dangling".
a boolean called 'scratch already exists' is false.
Create symbolic link from "procmissing1" to 'scratch dangling path'.
On error Set 'scratch already exists' to true.
If 'scratch already exists' is false then, Print "ASSERT PRC-28: expected 1 got {'scratch already exists'}", Exit 95. Print 'scratch already exists'.
Delete the file 'scratch link path'.
Delete the file 'scratch dangling path'.
Delete the file scratch.

--- PRC-42, 43, 44, 46: fork/reap basic ---
a number called 'loading bay' is fork.
If 'loading bay' is 0 then, Exit 29.
a number called 'loading bay reaped pid' is reap any child process.
a boolean called 'loading bay reap matched' is false.
If 'loading bay reaped pid' is 'loading bay' then, Set 'loading bay reap matched' to true.
If 'loading bay reap matched' is false then, Print "ASSERT PRC-46: expected 1 got {'loading bay reap matched'}", Exit 95. Print 'loading bay reap matched'.

--- the same leaf, a seed that draws the direct If-condition shape ---
If fork the process is 0 then, Exit 29.
a number called toolbox is reap any child process.
a boolean called 'toolbox reap succeeded' is false.
If toolbox is greater than 0 then, Set 'toolbox reap succeeded' to true.
If 'toolbox reap succeeded' is false then, Print "ASSERT PRC-42: expected 1 got {'toolbox reap succeeded'}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox reap succeeded'.

--- PRC-56, 57, 58: reaped status decode, first reap in program ---
If the reaped status is not -1 then, Print "ASSERT PRC-58: expected -1 got {the reaped status}", Exit 95. Print the reaped status.
a number called 'the message slip' is fork the process.
If 'the message slip' is 0 then, Exit 9.
a number called 'the message slip reap result' is reap child 'the message slip'.
a number called 'the message slip decoded exit' is the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256.
If 'the message slip decoded exit' is not 9 then, Print "ASSERT PRC-56: expected 9 got {'the message slip decoded exit'}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip decoded exit'.
a boolean called 'the message slip reap failed' is false.
a number called 'the message slip foreign reap' is reap process 9496391.
On error Set 'the message slip reap failed' to true.
If 'the message slip reap failed' is false then, Print "ASSERT PRC-49: expected 1 got {'the message slip reap failed'}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip reap failed'.
a number called 'the message slip still decoded' is the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256.
If 'the message slip still decoded' is not 9 then, Print "ASSERT PRC-57: expected 9 got {'the message slip still decoded'}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip still decoded'.

--- the same leaf, NOT the first reap: no sentinel claim ---
claims the -1 sentinel: 0
--- PRC-62, 63: status decode functions, first declaration ---
To 'exit code of' with a number called status.
    Return a number, status divide 256 modulo 256.

To 'signal of' with a number called status.
    Return a number, status bit-and 127.

a number called 'the sketchpad' is fork the process.
If 'the sketchpad' is 0 then, Exit 56.
a number called 'the sketchpad decode reap' is reap child 'the sketchpad'.
a number called 'the sketchpad status word' is the reaped status.
a number called 'the sketchpad manual exit' is 'the sketchpad status word' divide 256 modulo 256.
a number called 'the sketchpad function exit' is 'exit code of' of 'the sketchpad status word'.
If 'the sketchpad function exit' is not 'the sketchpad manual exit' then, Print "ASSERT PRC-63: expected {'the sketchpad manual exit'} got {'the sketchpad function exit'}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad function exit'.
If 'the sketchpad manual exit' is not 56 then, Print "ASSERT PRC-62: expected 56 got {'the sketchpad manual exit'}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad manual exit'.
a number called 'the sketchpad manual signal' is 'the sketchpad status word' bit-and 127.
a number called 'the sketchpad function signal' is 'signal of' of 'the sketchpad status word'.
If 'the sketchpad function signal' is not 'the sketchpad manual signal' then, Print "ASSERT PRC-63: expected {'the sketchpad manual signal'} got {'the sketchpad function signal'}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad function signal'.
If 'the sketchpad manual signal' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT PRC-62: expected 0 got {'the sketchpad manual signal'}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad manual signal'.

